      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T02:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s unclear what this parameter is for and what is intended to be passed to it.  You may have intended that it contain the hash of `data` as computed on line 383.  But actually `verity_fec_decode()` may have overwritten it with the unsuccessfully corrected data.\n\nIs this parameter actually necessary?  Since both `salt` and `data` are passed already, the hook implementation could hash them itself if it really needs to.  There are easy-to-use SHA-256 functions in `\u003ccrypto/sha2.h\u003e`.\n\nLikewise for `trace_android_vh_handle_data_error()`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 415,
