    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1add7c16_9641e23c",
        "filename": "drivers/md/dm-verity-target.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 415,
      "author": {
        "id": 4966542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T01:15:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The runtime digest is necessary for the Samsung debugging use case because we need to capture the digest actually produced by dm-verity at the time of the failure, rather than only being able to recompute it later from salt and data.\n\nOne of the cases we need to investigate is an AP-side computation malfunction. During failure analysis, we recompute the digest independently from the captured salt and data and compare it with the runtime digest produced by dm-verity. If we recompute the digest in the hook instead, we lose the original runtime result that we are trying to validate.\n\nFor PRE_FEC, io-\u003etmp_digest represents the digest from the initial verification failure and can also be saved as a fallback. After FEC has failed, however, the current io-\u003etmp_digest is diagnostically important because this is the final corruption state. Therefore, for the FEC_FAILED event, the intention is to use the post-FEC io-\u003etmp_digest when it still contains a meaningful digest for the failure being reported, and fall back to the saved PRE_FEC digest if FEC has overwritten it with an unusable value.",
